<abstract><p>This thesis asks whether the design of a social media radio platform can improve how university students judge what they hear, without losing the audience. It proposes LOKLOK and Epistemic Systems Theory, anchors a measured student wave (N = 52), reports a calibrated in-silico experiment (500 synthetic personas, 8 design cells, 18 sessions) with headline results of +0.827 on the evaluative rating and -0.183 engagement, triangulates the contrast across four assignment designs, and reports the machine-coding validation as the honest null result it is.</p></abstract>
