6.9.2
H2: Thermodynamic Diversity Eect (EST-P2)
The model reports ECO increasing by .035 and correction acceptance by .026. These
are conditional mechanism outputs. The eld interactionPB association measures
neither source-distribution entropy nor an echo-chamber trajectory, and cannot di-
rectly establish H2 or a thermodynamic constraint.
6.9.3
H3: Psychometric Validity (EST-P3)
The full validity claim in H3 is not established. EST-P3 remains a requirement to
test consequential metrics, not a declaration that these instruments have already sat-
ised that requirement. Instrument revision must preserve the distinction between
perceived credibility, perceived inuence, intention, and independently assessed con-
tent quality.
High internal consistency (α = 0.957 for the BRS) together with poor single-
factor CFA t is itself diagnostic: it can indicate redundant or overlapping items,</p>
<p>CHAPTER 6. RESULTS
183
unrelated method variance, or multidimensionality, and it is not evidence of a good
measurement model. Consistent with the calibrated appendix, the thesis therefore
reports reliability and structural validity separately, and the ne-grained factor ta-
bles are presented with their t indicators visible rather than optimised post hoc.
6.9.4
H4: EST Integration (EST-P1 to P3)
The positive associations are compatible with shared variation, but also with over-
lapping content or common response processes. The Bayesian coecient reported
later cannot resolve discriminant validity merely by assigning predictive weight to
IQ. H4 receives associational evidence, not conrmation of a unique latent cause.
6.9.5
H5 to H7: Exploratory and Prospective Hypotheses
H5 requires repeated participant or network observations to assess convergence, con-
sensus accuracy, or correction dynamics. H6 requires a design separating scheduling
from other causes of listening duration; ride duration is not necessarily attentive
listening time. H7 requires the planned independent appraisal and production as-
sessments on the agent platform. PB and star-rating dierences are not substitutes
for task performance. The present eld survey does not directly test these three
outcomes.
